# Check every text file out with LF line endings on every platform.
#
# Several tests compare a committed file byte-for-byte against generated text
# (`docs/nodes.md` vs the registry, generated `examples/*.ron` vs their builders).
# Git's default on Windows (core.autocrlf=true) rewrites those files to CRLF on
# checkout, so `include_str!` saw "\r\n" where the generator produced "\n" and the
# first Windows CI run failed `docs::tests::committed_docs_are_in_sync_with_the_registry`.
# Pinning eol=lf makes a checkout identical on macOS, Linux and Windows.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets never get line-ending conversion.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.wav binary
*.icns binary
*.ico binary
